# The companion who is narrating can die mid-phase, and the narration returns to the protagonist.
#
# The sharp edge of the standing death check. After a Speak-About hand-off the companion is the one
# who observes, deliberates and acts — and therefore the one a failed act's wound penalty lands on
# (see Chapter VI: every gate consults the acting body). So the member being narrated as is exactly
# the member who can be killed by the narration, and when they are, the phase is left with nobody to
# run it.
#
# NarrativeController.StartObservationPhaseWithHistory already answers that: an active member no
# longer in the party hands the narration back to the protagonist. This asserts the two halves
# together — the companion is really gone, and the session is still usable afterwards, which is what
# would break if the hand-off were left pointing at a corpse.
#
# The hand-off itself is companion_handoff.cli's subject; this repeats it as far as the companion's
# first act, which is what leaves the footer offering to open another segment rather than to leave
# the place — killing the cat before it has acted strands the session on a LEAVE, and the return of
# the narration is then unobservable. See companion_death_wounds.cli for the notice and the body,
# which are the same here and are not re-asserted.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# Speak About: keyword -> "Speak About" -> speaking modus mentis -> companion.
click keyword 0
choose 2
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

# The cat has the narration.
expect [NIGHTHUNTER]

# It takes its turn at the scene — its own observation, deliberation, act and dice.
strategy succeed
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# And is killed by what the narration deals out, being the body that was acting.
wound Nighthunter
wait 60

# The notice comes up with nothing clicked, over the narration.
expect Nighthunter
expect died of their wounds
click companion-death
wait 60

# Gone from the party...
inspect party
expect-no-state party Nighthunter
# ...and a body in the room they were narrating in.
inspect pois
expect-state pois Nighthunter's Remains

# The session survives them: the next segment opens with the protagonist narrating again, rather
# than on a member who is no longer in the party.
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

quit
